  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, the highest-priority question is establishing a clean, interpretable performance baseline. config_005 (RNA-only, single-profile, PCA-2000) is the simplest possible configuration: no learned encoder, no aggregation, no fusion. It will (1) provide a reference accuracy/F1 for the task using only transcriptomic data with a standard linear reduction, (2) serve as the anchor against which all future multimodal, multiprofile, or learned-encoder experiments can be compared to isolate the marginal contribution of each added design element, and (3) be fast to train, preserving budget for subsequent experiments. Starting here allows a systematic one-factor-at-a-time exploration: I can next vary the RNA encoder (scvi_n200, scgpt), add image modality, switch to multiprofile, or change aggregation/fusion, each time attributing performance shifts to a single change. This is the most information-efficient first step under a limited budget."
}

